{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUG AREA (Corvo addition)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Prints the area of a rug in square metres, without needless zeros: "3", "8.75", "4.08". Only the number is printed:
the unit comes from the sentence around it ("rug_page.area" in the locale file).

The area is rounded to two decimals, the same way the scripts of the rug page and of the price guide round it
(assets/rug-configurator.js and assets/rug-price-guide.js), so the page says the same number before and after they run.

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* width: the width of the rug, in centimetres (required)
* length: the length of the rug, in centimetres (required)
* shape: "round" for a round rug, whose width and length are both its diameter (optional)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign area_width = width | plus: 0
  assign area_length = length | plus: 0
  assign area_cm2 = area_width | times: area_length

  if shape == 'round'
    comment
      The area of a circle is its diameter squared × π / 4 (0.7854)
    endcomment

    assign area_cm2 = area_cm2 | times: 7854 | plus: 5000 | divided_by: 10000
  endif

  assign area_hundredths = area_cm2 | plus: 50 | divided_by: 100
  assign area_rest = area_hundredths | modulo: 100
  assign area_number = area_hundredths | divided_by: 100 | append: ''

  if area_rest > 0
    assign area_decimals = area_rest | append: ''
    assign area_rest_tens = area_rest | modulo: 10

    if area_rest_tens == 0
      assign area_decimals = area_rest | divided_by: 10 | append: ''
    elsif area_rest < 10
      assign area_decimals = area_rest | prepend: '0'
    endif

    assign area_number = area_number | append: '.' | append: area_decimals
  endif
-%}

{{- area_number -}}
